From d1a913b02096a55423008ab3527a521c4d2a93a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DisplayXR <dev@displayxr.invalid>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:17:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] inline-3d(#167): never weave a tile that emitted no quad this
 frame

An opaque sticky page header was interlaced whenever a woven tile scrolled
underneath it -- reported as "the words Account and Sign in get woven", which
is the whole bar: a flat colour interlaces to itself, so only the glyphs show
it.

MEASURED, on the reported page, at the moment the bar was woven (installed
0.1.19, Leia panel, --v=1):

  ID-MATCH FALLBACK: reason=layer_id stamped but NO quad anywhere in the frame
    carries it -- the layer emitted no SharedQuadState ...
    id=FE66...0013 layer_id=39 target=2351,358 1100x120 among 28 quads
    (0 diagnostic-only), elsewhere=0 pass=0
  plane-split: tiles=1 quads=31 over_set=0 tiles_without_k=1 excluded{...all 0}
  GPU canvas-layer lookup returned NO resource: id=FE66...0013
    rect=2351,358 1100x120 layers=0 (misses=1000)
  batch weave: n=1 ... eyes_valid=1 flat=0

Every frame, not intermittently: 1000 misses and the batch still carrying the
rect. Page state at that instant (CDP): dpr 2.5, `#site-header` sticky,
`rgb(18,23,21)`, backdrop-filter NONE, 0..106 CSS px; the tile's canvas at
y=-392 h=440, i.e. 48 CSS px still on screen (48 * 2.5 = the 120 device px in
the rect) and ALL of it under the bar. x/width map to the right-hand end of the
header -- where "Account / Sign in" sit.

MECHANISM. The tile is FULLY OCCLUDED by the opaque header, so cc drops its
layer from the drawn list and it emits no SharedQuadState at all. No quad ->
no canvas resource -> nothing suppressed from the page raster, and the rect
still arrives from CollectTrackedElementRects, which walks the whole active
tree. browser#117's lockstep gate then hits its own escape --

    bool prepared = resolved_canvas.empty();

-- because this page has ONE tile, so "nothing resolved at all this frame" is
true, the rect is submitted, and the GPU stage (layers=0, the same escape
one stage later) snapshots |output| at the rect as the weave source. That
snapshot is the header. The runtime weaves it and draws it back over itself.

So browser#117 diagnosed this exact corruption -- its own report was the
gallery's title coming back interlaced from a tile clipped to a strip under a
sticky header -- and closed every route to it EXCEPT the one a single-tile page
takes. Whether an unrelated sibling tile happened to resolve cannot be what
decides if the runtime weaves page chrome.

The plane split cannot help here and no CSS on the header can either. The
split needs k, the canvas quad's index in the live root list, and there is no
canvas quad anywhere; tiles_without_k=1 for the whole session. Both CSS
workarounds tried on the issue (opaque + blur(0px), opaque + blur(8px)) failed
on hardware for that reason, and the four-configuration matrix in the issue is
moot: this fires for any header opaque enough to occlude, filtered or not.

THE FIX, in the one place that has the evidence.

(1) surface_aggregator.cc -- an element whose layer id is carried by NO quad
    anywhere in the frame (`elsewhere == 0`, the census browser#117 added) is
    marked on the frame, and the geometric fallback is skipped for it. That
    skip is browser#94's argument verbatim, which already reaches the same
    conclusion one branch up from a viewport test: an element that contributed
    no quad cannot be matched to one, so any quad clearing the overlap bar is a
    stranger's, and adopting it would suppress the stranger's resource and hand
    the weave the wrong pixels.

(2) display.cc -- the "nothing resolved at all" escape no longer applies to a
    tile marked that way. The rect is withheld from the batch, counted on the
    existing LOG(ERROR) with its own sub-count, and the tile simply does not
    weave for those frames.

(3) direct_renderer.cc -- comment only. The `!k.has_value()` continue still
    claimed "Phase-1 behaviour, i.e. the page keeps painting over it"; Phase 1
    was deleted by 0065, so that sentence described a fallback that no longer
    exists. It now says what the two upstream gates guarantee and what
    tiles_without_k is still worth reading for.

WHAT DOES NOT CHANGE. An element with `elsewhere > 0` -- drawn, but by a quad
in a pass the identity join does not search -- is in the page raster, so it
keeps both the geometric fallback and the legacy snapshot weave. The legacy
no-identity channel (`sqs_layer_id == 0`) is not censused and is untouched. The
browser#94 offscreen branch returns before any of this.

THE TRADE, stated: a tile whose resource is not ready also emits no quad, and
now stops weaving for those frames instead of weaving the page behind it. That
is the same direction web#12 and browser#117 both chose -- the page draws what
it drew, and the runtime never weaves content that is not the tile's.

NOT DONE HERE: samples/composition still has no opaque-sticky-bar-over-a-
scrolling-tile case, which is why this shipped. It belongs in displayxr-web
alongside this.
---
 .../viz/service/display/aggregated_frame.h    | 19 +++++++
 .../viz/service/display/direct_renderer.cc    | 28 +++++++++--
 components/viz/service/display/display.cc     | 33 ++++++++++++-
 .../viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc | 49 ++++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/aggregated_frame.h b/components/viz/service/display/aggregated_frame.h
index f996438..e7bab1b 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/aggregated_frame.h
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/aggregated_frame.h
@@ -110,6 +110,25 @@ class VIZ_SERVICE_EXPORT AggregatedFrame {
     // the root pass does not draw.
     static constexpr size_t kUnknownZOrder = static_cast<size_t>(-1);
     size_t z_order = kUnknownZOrder;
+    // browser#167: this element's layer emitted NO SharedQuadState anywhere in
+    // the frame — no quad in any pass, admissible or diagnostic-only, carries
+    // its (namespace, layer id). It contributed nothing to the page raster, so
+    // the composited output at |rect| holds SOMEONE ELSE'S pixels: whatever
+    // occluded the element out of the drawn layer list (an opaque sticky
+    // header over the last strip of a scrolling tile), or what was behind it
+    // while its resource was not ready.
+    //
+    // The weave must therefore not touch the rect — snapshotting the page
+    // there and weaving it interlaces that other content. Consumed by
+    // Display::DrawAndSwap, which cannot re-derive this: the absence of a
+    // canvas resource for the tile is indistinguishable there from a page that
+    // has no canvas-resource channel at all.
+    //
+    // False whenever the aggregator has no such evidence — the legacy
+    // main-thread channel (no layer id to census), and an element that IS
+    // drawn by a quad in a pass the identity join does not search. Both keep
+    // every pre-browser#167 behaviour.
+    bool layer_emitted_no_quad = false;
   };
   std::vector<Inline3dTrackedRect> inline_3d_rects;
 
diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/direct_renderer.cc b/components/viz/service/display/direct_renderer.cc
index 75e50b6..07a49c9 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/direct_renderer.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/direct_renderer.cc
@@ -737,9 +737,31 @@ void DirectRenderer::ComputeInline3dPlaneSplit(
     }
     if (!k.has_value()) {
       // No quad for this tile in the live list (promoted to an overlay, removed
-      // as overdraw, or no canvas resource id was resolvable). Skip the split
-      // for this tile — Phase-1 behaviour, i.e. the page keeps painting over
-      // it. Risk guard R1.
+      // as overdraw, or no canvas resource id was resolvable), so there is no
+      // paint position to split the page at. Skip the split for this tile.
+      // Risk guard R1.
+      //
+      // (browser#167) THE OLD WORDING HERE — "Phase-1 behaviour, i.e. the page
+      // keeps painting over it" — DESCRIBED A FALLBACK THAT NO LONGER EXISTS.
+      // Phase 1 was deleted by the patch that made occlusion the only
+      // mechanism, so "the page keeps painting over it" now means the over-tile
+      // content stays in the page raster AND the pre-blend feeds that raster to
+      // the weave as the tile's backdrop: not a fallback, an artefact.
+      //
+      // What keeps that harmless is upstream, not here. A tile reaches this
+      // point with no |k| in two shapes, and the weave has already been
+      // withheld for both by the time the split runs:
+      //   * the element emitted no quad at all this frame — the aggregator's
+      //     census marks it and Display::DrawAndSwap keeps its rect out of the
+      //     batch (browser#167);
+      //   * its canvas resource did not resolve — the same gate, one clause
+      //     earlier (browser#117).
+      // A tile that IS woven therefore always has a canvas quad in some pass,
+      // and the only way to arrive here still weaving is the case browser#117
+      // withdrew for want of evidence: the quad living in a child pass this
+      // scan does not walk. |tiles_without_k| stays the counter that would say
+      // so — read it together with the ID-MATCH FALLBACK line's |elsewhere|,
+      // which names which of the two shapes it is.
       ++tiles_without_k;
       continue;
     }
diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/display.cc b/components/viz/service/display/display.cc
index 28d5d79..a1408f5 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/display.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/display.cc
@@ -1085,8 +1085,31 @@ bool Display::DrawAndSwap(const DrawAndSwapParams& params) {
       std::vector<SkiaOutputSurface::Inline3dRect> weave_rects;
       weave_rects.reserve(frame.inline_3d_rects.size());
       int unprepared = 0;
+      int unprepared_undrawn = 0;
       for (const auto& r : frame.inline_3d_rects) {
-        bool prepared = resolved_canvas.empty();
+        // ---- (browser#167) THE "NOTHING RESOLVED AT ALL" ESCAPE IS NOT FOR A
+        // TILE THAT WAS NEVER DRAWN --------------------------------------
+        //
+        // The escape below says: with no canvas resource anywhere this frame,
+        // nothing was suppressed either, so the page raster at |rect| is the
+        // tile's own drawing and snapshotting it is the legitimate
+        // pre-browser#18 weave source. True — but ONLY while the tile is
+        // actually in that raster.
+        //
+        // |layer_emitted_no_quad| is the aggregator's census saying it is not:
+        // no quad anywhere in the frame carries this element's layer id, so it
+        // painted nothing, and |rect| holds whatever occluded it. On the
+        // reported page that is an opaque sticky header, and the weave
+        // interlaced its glyphs ("Account / Sign in") every frame the tile's
+        // last strip spent underneath it.
+        //
+        // Note what makes this the SINGLE-TILE hole in browser#117's law: with
+        // a second tile on the page |resolved_canvas| is non-empty, the escape
+        // never fires, and the rect is already withheld. Whether an unrelated
+        // sibling happens to have resolved cannot be what decides if the
+        // runtime weaves page chrome — so the undrawn tile is withheld either
+        // way now.
+        bool prepared = resolved_canvas.empty() && !r.layer_emitted_no_quad;
         for (const auto& layer : resolved_canvas) {
           // Identity where there is one; the legacy zero-id channel has only
           // geometry, and Display's own tile join above uses the same pair of
@@ -1098,6 +1121,9 @@ bool Display::DrawAndSwap(const DrawAndSwapParams& params) {
         }
         if (!prepared) {
           ++unprepared;
+          if (r.layer_emitted_no_quad) {
+            ++unprepared_undrawn;
+          }
           continue;
         }
         // browser#131: |z_order| rides along untouched — the GPU stage's
@@ -1116,7 +1142,10 @@ bool Display::DrawAndSwap(const DrawAndSwapParams& params) {
                      << " of " << frame.inline_3d_rects.size()
                      << " weave rects: no canvas resource resolved, so the page"
                         " still owns those pixels and the weave must not touch"
-                        " them (withheld="
+                        " them (of which "
+                     << unprepared_undrawn
+                     << " emitted no quad at all this frame (browser#167);"
+                        " withheld="
                      << (n + 1) << ")";
         }
       }
diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
index 1250565..69921fe 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
@@ -2711,7 +2711,12 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
   }
   // Phase-1 identity: match each inline-3d canvas rect to the resource quad
   // that draws it by IDENTITY first, geometry only as a fallback.
-  for (const Inline3dTrackedRect& canvas : inline_3d_rects_) {
+  // browser#167: indexed, because the verdict below has to be written back
+  // onto the frame's copy of this element. |frame.inline_3d_rects| was filled
+  // from |inline_3d_rects_| in order, one entry each, just above — so the two
+  // are index-parallel by construction.
+  for (size_t ci = 0; ci < inline_3d_rects_.size(); ++ci) {
+    const Inline3dTrackedRect& canvas = inline_3d_rects_[ci];
     std::optional<RootResourceQuad> m = id_match(canvas, root_resource_quads_);
     if (!m) {
       // browser#94 — the OFFSCREEN-BUT-REGISTERED tile: an expected absence,
@@ -2813,6 +2818,48 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
                 << " diagnostic-only), elsewhere=" << elsewhere << " pass="
                 << (elsewhere ? elsewhere_pass.GetUnsafeValue() : 0u);
       }
+      // ---- (browser#167) AN ELEMENT THAT EMITTED NO QUAD IS NOT IN THIS
+      // FRAME ------------------------------------------------------------
+      //
+      // |elsewhere| == 0 with a layer id stamped is the strongest verdict this
+      // function can reach: NOTHING in the frame — root pass, child pass,
+      // admissible or diagnostic-only — carries this element's
+      // (namespace, layer id). The layer emitted no SharedQuadState, so it
+      // contributed no pixels to the page raster: it is not in the drawn layer
+      // list (fully OCCLUDED, e.g. the last strip of a tile scrolling under an
+      // opaque sticky header — browser#167's report) or its resource is not
+      // ready.
+      //
+      // Two consequences, and they are the same argument browser#94 already
+      // makes one branch up for the offscreen tile, which is this condition
+      // with a viewport test instead of a quad census:
+      //
+      //   1. THE GEOMETRIC FALLBACK MUST NOT RUN. This element contributed no
+      //      quad by construction, so any quad clearing the overlap bar
+      //      against its rect is a DIFFERENT element's. Adopting it would add
+      //      that stranger's resource to the suppression set in
+      //      Display::DrawAndSwap — punching an on-screen hole the weave never
+      //      fills — and hand the weave the wrong pixels for this token.
+      //
+      //   2. THE WEAVE MUST NOT TOUCH THE RECT. Say so on the frame, because
+      //      Display::DrawAndSwap cannot re-derive it: with no canvas resource
+      //      for this tile AND none for any other tile on the page, browser#117
+      //      falls through its "nothing resolved at all this frame" escape and
+      //      submits the rect anyway. That escape is sound only where it was
+      //      written — the legacy no-identity channel, where the page raster
+      //      IS the tile's own drawing. Here the page raster at |rect| is
+      //      whatever occluded the tile, and weaving it interlaces that
+      //      content: the reported "Account / Sign in get woven". A single-tile
+      //      page is the whole exposure, which is why this survived
+      //      browser#117 — there, a sibling tile always resolved.
+      //
+      // An element with |elsewhere| > 0 is drawn, just not where the join
+      // looks; its pixels ARE in the page raster, so it keeps both the
+      // geometric fallback and the legacy snapshot weave, unchanged.
+      if (canvas.sqs_layer_id != 0 && elsewhere == 0) {
+        frame.inline_3d_rects[ci].layer_emitted_no_quad = true;
+        continue;
+      }
       // browser#117: the fallback compares on the COMMON visible space, so a
       // tile that is only partly on screen scores against its own quad exactly
       // as a fully visible one does.
